WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.403
-I'm so happy
that you're here in studio.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:05.538
-I believe you.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.006
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:10.076
Last time you were on, I got you
to Zoom, which was unbelievable.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.879
That'll never happen again
in the history of my lifetime,

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.080
will I get you on Zoom.
-No. No.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.648
That's correct.
-And I loved that.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.483
I love that that happened
for me, just as a --

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.919
It's the little wins
that make me happy.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.987
But we talked about
"Pretend It's a City,"

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:26.759
which is a great miniseries
on Netflix.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.929
If you just -- If you just
want to laugh, just put this on.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:33.733
You are so observant and have
a different view of everything

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.370
wherever you go, from crossing
the street to anything.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.638
Is there anything happening now
in New York City

00:00:39.638 --> 00:00:42.408
that you're going, like,
"Okay, I'm noticing this"?

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:45.645
-I did notice that the very
first thing that came back,

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.480
months ago, was traffic.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.382
[ Laughter ]
Okay? So, there's like --

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.784
No one is here.
There's nowhere to go.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.986
Everything's closed.
No one's working.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:56.255
No one's going to school.
Nothing is open.

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:58.324
There's no place to go,
but there was just traffic.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.992
[ Laughter ]
-No place -- That is true.

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:02.028
-I thought this is kind of,
you know,

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.796
traffic in its purest form,

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.332
you know, traffic
with no purpose at all.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.469
It's just, you know, traffic
that was probably sent here

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.304
by a hostile foreign power.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.106
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.907
Just traffic sitting there,

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:17.810
and of course, everyone
was driving very recklessly,

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.312
honking the horns.
I think, "Where you going?

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:21.814
What's the big rush?

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:22.849
There's nowhere to go."

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:23.917
-There's actually nowhere to go.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.117
That's the first thing
to come back.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:26.852
-Right. So traffic was
first thing to come back.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:30.223
-What do you think about
legalization of marijuana?

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:34.260
-You know, I haven't taken drugs
since I was 19,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.195
but I don't care
what other people do at all.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.529
But it does seem to me

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:39.833
since it was legalized
for recreational use --

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.034
I love that term,
"recreational use" --

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:46.505
It seems that it wasn't
just legalized, it seems --

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:49.175
made legal -- it seems like
it was made mandatory.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.510
You know.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:56.416
The streets of New York
are clouds of weed.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.617
You can't -- If you don't
want to smoke marijuana,

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.753
you have no choice,
you know, basically.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.622
-It is unbelievable.
-Every single person.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.056
-Everyone is, yeah.
-Except me.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:05.191
-Yeah. Yeah, me, too.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.526
You walk by a construction site,
and it is the --

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:09.628
-And that's really shocking,
because there they are.

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:11.063
They're hanging
from these beams,

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.632
and I think, you know,

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.833
it's not me
that's going to fall, you know?

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:16.002
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.703
How high do you want to be?

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:18.871
Yeah, there you go.

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.439
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:22.908
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:25.178
Now, I want to give this a plug

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.646
even though you're not here
to plug anything,

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.280
which, you're just here
because you're a good friend.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.882
But this is
"The Fran Lebowitz Reader,"

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:33.018
and I encourage anyone
to get this, if you get this,

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:36.388
because it is exactly this
funny, and it's a great read,

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:39.859
and I just never get a chance
to plug anything for you.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.495
But I know you're back
doing shows.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.829
You're doing -- You do shows

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:45.932
where someone interviews you
for 30 minutes,

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.933
and then you answer questions
with the audience.

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:49.969
-Right, someone interviews me
on a stage...

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.771
-Yeah.
-...for 30 minutes.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.172
And then they leave.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.373
-Mm.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.342
-Just mentioning. Just saying.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.610
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.712
And then I go to a lectern,

00:03:00.712 --> 00:03:03.015
and I answer questions
from the audience for an hour.

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:04.951
-That's, so, April 6th and 7th,

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.786
you're at a town hall
here in New York.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.121
So everyone has to go to this,

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:10.556
'cause this will be
unbelievable.

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.424
You get to see Fran Lebowitz
in person.

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:15.295
For information, which is --
This is great, again --

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.264
there is not yet a website
currently, 'cause this is Fran.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.632
So, you're on your Facebook.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.802
Facebook.com/FranLebowitz.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.169
We're going to put it
on the thing.

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:25.871
How did you end up
even setting that up?

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:27.606
-I didn't.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.606 --> 00:03:29.408
I didn't -- I've never seen it.

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:31.410
My agent did it. It's like --

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.413
By the way,
I've never seen Netflix.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.580
-Yeah.
-I've never seen it.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.182
And when I --
this was coming out,

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.117
I would ask people,
"Do you have Netflix?"

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.518
And they would look at me
like I was asking,

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:42.054
"Do you have electricity?"
Because apparently there's

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:43.889
one person in the country
that doesn't have Netflix.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.524
That's me.
-Yeah. We love you.

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:48.594
Come back whenever and Zoom me
whenever you want to.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.663
-I won't, don't worry.
-Fran Lebowitz, everybody!

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.498
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.067
Oh, I want to show --
Let me show a clip.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.669
I want to show a clip
of the show.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:59.037
Here's a clip of Fran
in "Pretend It's a City."

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:01.374
Take a look at this.
-I don't know if they do to you

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.675
where you have your own,
actually, young child.

00:04:03.675 --> 00:04:04.977
I didn't mean a little child,
but a teenager.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.278
-Yes. Yes.

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.847
-But people that age,
the age of your daughter --

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:10.716
-Yes.
-...and somewhat older,

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:12.951
very often approach me

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:15.821
to ask me my opinion
of what they should do in life.

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.357
Like, you know, "Fran --"
And I just think, like,

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.392
first of all,
I don't care what you do.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.026
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:22.128
They're so used to being, like,

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.462
the center
of their parents' attention,

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:25.631
that anyone they see that age,
they just think, like,

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:28.267
you know, "Maybe this person
will help me out."

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.369
But that would be a mistake
with me, because --

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:31.570
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:35.073
-That is so exactly
on the money.

00:04:35.073 --> 00:04:36.709
Fran Lebowitz, everybody!

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.812
Check out this book, by the way,
"The Fran Lebowitz Reader."

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:43.048
"Pretend It's a City"
is on Netflix now.

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:44.950
Go to Fran's Facebook page
for more info

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.421
to see her live in town hall!
She's all over.

